Which files this covers

  * Every source file (Python, JavaScript, shell, PowerShell, HTML, CSS and the
    Windows setup script) carries the line
    "SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later" near its top. A test
    (tools/freeform_studio/tests/test_license_headers.py) fails if a new one is
    added without it.
  * Documentation and images are covered by the same license as the rest of
    the project.
  * One file also follows an Apache-2.0 original and says so in its own header:
    tools/patch_voice_for_sherpa_onnx.py. The Apache-2.0 text is in
    LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt.

Where this came from

  This repository was split out of ACK (the phone app, in its own repository).
  The history of ACK Voice Studio's own files was kept. Freeform Studio and the
  voice-training helpers it depends on were copied in as one snapshot; the same
  copyright line and license apply to them.

Other people's software

